    "question": "A company needs to build a disaster recovery (DR) solution for its ecommerce website. The web application is hosted on a eet of t3.large Amazon EC2 instances and uses an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance. The EC2 instances are in an Auto Scaling group that extends across multiple Availability Zones. In the event of a disaster, the web application must fail over to the secondary environment with an RPO of 30 seconds and an RTO of 10 minutes. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
