    "question": "A company is creating a REST API to share information with six of its partners based in the United States. The company has created an Amazon API Gateway Regional endpoint. Each of the six partners will access the API once per day to post daily sales gures. After initial deployment, the company observes 1,000 requests per second originating from 500 different IP addresses around the world. The company believes this tra c is originating from a botnet and wants to secure its API while minimizing cost. Which approach should the company take to secure its API?",
