    "question": "A company uses AWS CloudFormation to deploy applications within multiple VPCs that are all attached to a transit gateway. Each VPC that sends tra c to the public internet must send the tra c through a shared services VPC. Each subnet within a VPC uses the default VPC route table, and the tra c is routed to the transit gateway. The transit gateway uses its default route table for any VPC attachment. A security audit reveals that an Amazon EC2 instance that is deployed within a VPC can communicate with an EC2 instance that is deployed in any of the company's other VPCs. A solutions architect needs to limit the tra c between the VPCs. Each VPC must be able to communicate only with a prede ned, limited set of authorized VPCs. What should the solutions architect do to meet these requirements?",
    "question_zh": "一家公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 在多个 VPC 中部署应用程序，所有这些VPC 都连接到中转网关。每个向公共互联网发送流量的VPC都必须透过共享服务VPC发送流量。 VPC 内的每个子网路都使用预设的 VPC 路由表，并且流量将路由到中转网关。中转网关对任何 VPC 连接使用其预设路由表。安全审核显示，部署在 VPC 中的 Amazon EC2 实例可以与部署在公司任何其他 VPC 中的 EC2 实例进行通讯。解决方案架构师需要限制VPC之间的流量。每个VPC 必须只能与一组预先定义的、有限的授权VPC 进行通讯。解决方案架构师应该怎么做才能满足这些要求？",
