    "question": "A company hosts a data-processing application on Amazon EC2 instances. The application polls an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) le system for newly uploaded les. When a new le is detected, the application extracts data from the le and runs logic to select a Docker container image to process the le. The application starts the appropriate container image and passes the le location as a parameter. The data processing that the container performs can take up to 2 hours. When the processing is complete, the code that runs inside the container writes the le back to Amazon EFS and exits. The company needs to refactor the application to eliminate the EC2 instances that are running the containers. Which solution will meet these requirements?",
